You see a woman dressed in a white lab coat, standing around with her hands in her pockets.
The id-card on her lapel says “Dr. Wisteria - General Practitioner - Star Hospital”. 
There are some dark red stains at the bottom of her coat that imply she may do some more practical medicine than just consulting.
She gives you a quick look up and down as you approach, before resuming looking around at nothing in particular.
